rix / CycEnv > Pitch 1+2", "+40 (est.)"], ["Envelope / A D S R", "0 / 35 / 0 / 20"], ["Voice / Mode", "Mono"], ["Voice / Glide", "0 (off)"]], "seq": "Four on the floor at C1 for EBM and industrial; for hip hop, C1 on beat 1 and the 'and' of 3.", "play": "A punchy, distorted synth kick. Fall sets the click-to-boom sweep and Decay sets the length.", "source": "https://solidtrax.nl/arturia-minifreak-review/", "sourceName": "Built from: Solidtrax (short cycling envelope for percussion)"}, {"name": "Sheet Metal Snare", "category": "Perc", "settings": [["Osc 1 / Type", "Noise"], ["Osc 1 / Wave (Type)", "white region (est.)"], ["Osc 1 / Timbre (Rate)", "70"], ["Osc 1 / Shape (Balance)", "30"], ["Osc 2 / Type", "Modal"], ["Osc 2 / Wave (Inharm)", "70"], ["Osc 2 / Shape (Decay)", "20"], ["Osc 2 / Volume", "50"], ["Filter / Type", "HP"], ["Filter / Cutoff", "30"], ["Filter / Resonance", "20"], ["FX 1 / Type", "Distortion - Climb, gain 30, Amount 30"], ["FX 2 / Type", "Reverb - Room, Time 30, Amount 25"], ["Envelope / A D S R", "0 / 20 / 0 / 15"], ["Voice / Mode", "Poly"]], "seq": "Play it at D2.", "play": "A noise crack plus a clanky modal body, like hitting a steel plate. Raise Inharm for more metal, lengthen Decay for a gated industrial feel.", "source": "https://forums.musicplayer.com/topic/184514-in-the-lab-arturia-minifreak-v-and-minifreak-redux/", "sourceName": "Built from: MPN GearLab Noise and Modal notes"}, {"name": "Ferric Hat", "category": "Perc", "settings": [["Osc 1 / Type", "Noise"], ["Osc 1 / Wave (Type)", "metallic region (est.)"], ["Osc 1 / Timbre (Rate)", "80"], ["Osc 1 / Shape (Balance)", "0"], ["Osc 2 / Volume", "0"], ["Filter / Type", "HP"], ["Filter / Cutoff", "80"], ["Filter / Resonance", "15"], ["FX 1 / Type", "Bit Crusher, Amount 20"], ["Envelope / A D S R", "0 / 8 / 0 / 8"], ["Matrix / Velocity > Envelope Decay", "+20"], ["Voice / Mode", "Poly"]], "seq": "Sequencer at 1/16 on one note, alternating high and low velocity; Spice adds random gate and decay variation.", "play": "A tight metallic tick that velocity opens toward an open hat. Run it from the sequencer with Spice for live hat variation.", "source": "https://forums.musicplayer.com/topic/184514-in-the-lab-arturia-minifreak-v-and-minifreak-redux/", "sourceName": "Built from: MPN GearLab Noise engine + Spice notes"}, {"name": "Radio Exorcism", "category": "FX", "settings": [["Osc 1 / Type", "Speech"], ["Osc 1 / Wave (Type)", "radio/techy word bank (est.)"], ["Osc 1 / Timbre", "50"], ["Osc 1 / Shape (Word)", "30"], ["Osc 2 / Type", "Multi Filter"], ["Osc 2 / Wave (Cutoff)", "50"], ["Osc 2 / Timbre (Resonance)", "40"], ["Osc 2 / Shape (Mode)", "BP (est.)"], ["Osc 2 / Volume", "80 (dry/wet)"], ["Filter / Type", "BP"], ["Filter / Cutoff", "55"], ["Filter / Resonance", "20"], ["FX 1 / Type", "Bit Crusher, Amount 30"], ["FX 2 / Type", "Delay - Filtered Ping-Pong Sync, 1/8D, Intensity 50, Amount 30"], ["FX 3 / Type", "Reverb - Hall, Time 75, Amount 40"], ["LFO 2 / Wave + Rate", "SnH, 1/8 synced, Retrig Free"], ["Matrix / LFO 2 > Osc 1 Shape (Word)", "+40"], ["Envelope / A D S R", "0 / - / 100 / 40"], ["Voice / Mode", "Mono"]], "seq": "", "play": "Garbled, band-limited robot words jumping at random like a haunted shortwave set. Hold a note and change the LFO 2 rate for faster or slower babble.", "source": "https://forums.musicplayer.com/topic/184514-in-the-lab-arturia-minifreak-v-and-minifreak-redux/", "sourceName": "Built from: MPN GearLab Speech engine notes"}, {"name": "Falling Bolts", "category": "FX", "settings": [["Osc 1 / Type", "Modal"], ["Osc 1 / Wave (Inharm)", "60"], ["Osc 1 / Shape (Decay)", "20"], ["Osc 2 / Volume", "0"], ["Filter / Type", "LP"], ["Filter / Cutoff", "70"], ["FX 1 / Type", "Reverb - Echoes, Time 50, Amount 35"], ["Cycling Env / Mode", "Loop"], ["Cycling Env / Rise / Fall", "0 / 40"], ["Matrix / CycEnv > VCA", "+100"], ["LFO 2 / Wave + Rate", "ExpSaw, 0.3 Hz, Retrig One"], ["Matrix / LFO 2 > Cycling Env Fall", "-40 (est.)"], ["Envelope / A D S R", "0 / - / 100 / 60"], ["Voice / Mode", "Mono"]], "seq": "", "play": "A bouncing-ball effect: the hits repeat faster and faster as the loop shortens, like scrap metal settling. Change the LFO 2 rate to set how long the bounce lasts.", "source": "https://www.guitarcenter.com/riffs/interviews/keyboards--midi/arturia-mini-freak", "sourceName": "Built from: Guitar Center Riffs bouncing-ball tip"}, {"name": "Ninth Ward Arp", "category": "Sequence", "settings": [["Osc 1 / Type", "BasicWaves"], ["Osc 1 / Wave (Morph)", "0 (square)"], ["Osc 1 / Timbre (Sym)", "40"], ["Osc 2 / Type", "Surgeon Filter"], ["Osc 2 / Wave (Cutoff)", "55"], ["Osc 2 / Timbre (Spread)", "30"], ["Osc 2 / Shape (Mode)", "BP (est.)"], ["Osc 2 / Volume", "70 (dry/wet)"], ["Filter / Type", "LP"], ["Filter / Cutoff", "45"], ["Filter / Resonance", "30"], ["Filter / Env Amt", "+35"], ["FX 1 / Type", "Delay - Ping-Pong Sync, 3/16, Intensity 40, Amount 30"], ["FX 2 / Type", "Reverb - Dark Room, Time 50, Amount 25"], ["Envelope / A D S R", "0 / 30 / 0 / 25"], ["Voice / Mode", "Poly"], ["Arp / Mode", "Walk"], ["Arp / Rate + Gate", "1/16, Gate 40"], ["Arp / Octave", "2"], ["Arp / Modifier", "Rand Oct on, Ratchet now and then"], ["Seq / Mod lane 1", "Filter Cutoff, slow rising ramp over 16 steps"]], "seq": "Hold A C E F with Arp Hold; Walk keeps it wandering around the root.", "play": "A nervous, hollow arpeggio for darksynth intros and horror cues. Spice adds random gates and octaves; hit Dice for a new variation.", "source": "https://forums.musicplayer.com/topic/184514-in-the-lab-arturia-minifreak-v-and-minifreak-redux/", "sourceName": "Built from: MPN GearLab arp tips (Walk, Spice/Dice)"}, {"name": "Robot Mass", "category": "Texture", "settings": [["Osc 1 / Type", "SawX"], ["Osc 1 / Wave (SawMod)", "50"], ["Osc 1 / Timbre (Shape)", "40"], ["Osc 1 / Shape (Noise)", "15"], ["Osc 2 / Type", "Chords"], ["Osc 2 / Wave (Interval)", "minor (est.)"], ["Osc 2 / Timbre (Inv/Trsp)", "30"], ["Osc 2 / Volume", "60"], ["Filter / Type", "LP"], ["Filter / Cutoff", "60"], ["Filter / Resonance", "15"], ["FX 1 / Type", "Vocoder Self - Gated (Shift+Type for the subtype)"], ["FX 1 / Time + Intensity", "Spectrum 50, Formant Shift -30 (est.)"], ["FX 1 / Amount", "70"], ["FX 2 / Type", "Chorus - Dark, Amount 25"], ["FX 3 / Type", "Reverb - Hall, Time 70, Amount 40"], ["LFO 1 / Wave + Rate", "Shaper (draw a 16-step rhythmic gate), 1/16 synced, Retrig Mono Kbd"], ["Matrix / LFO 1 > Osc 2 Timbre (Inv/Trsp)", "+30"], ["Envelope / A D S R", "30 / - / 90 / 50"], ["Voice / Mode", "Mono"], ["Voice / Glide", "0 (off)"]], "seq": "", "play": "A choir of machines: chord stacks through the built-in vocoder with shifting inversions. Formant Shift is the key knob; negative values sound bigger and more sinister.", "source": "https://www.arturia.com/products/hardware-synths/minifreak/update", "sourceName": "Built from: Arturia Vocoder Self notes + manual Chords params"}]